        }
      ],
      "title": "Input Text (Prompt)",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveStringMultiline"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Cinematic science-fiction industrial sequence, 16:9 widescreen, 10 seconds, premium photorealistic VFX, dramatic but clean white-and-warm-gold lighting.\n\n<Picture 1> defines the NVIDIA RTX 2000 Ada GPU hardware design used for both robots: matte-black GPU armor, rear blower fan, metal ventilation grille, PCIe gold contacts, and precise mechanical details.\n\n<Picture 2> defines the Raylight logo.\n\n<Picture 3> defines the MiniMax logo.\n\n<Picture 4> defines the dark neon technological environment, but transform it into a brighter futuristic weaving chamber with a luminous ivory-white background, subtle green energy lines, and warm golden reflections.\n\n<Picture 5> defines the appearance, body proportions, and symmetrical placement of the two transformer-like robots.\n\n[Shot 1] Two transformer-like robots built from the hardware features of <Picture 1> stand opposite each other beside a futuristic mechanical loom. Their full bodies are already transformed at the beginning of the shot. The camera begins in a high overhead wide shot and rapidly descends into a dynamic three-quarter top view.\n\nBoth robots immediately operate the loom using their articulated mechanical hands. Their fingers precisely grab, pull, cross, and tighten hundreds of glowing golden threads. The hand motions must clearly resemble real fabric weaving rather than welding, firing energy, or simply touching the cloth. Small gears rotate inside their wrists, finger joints rapidly articulate, spindles turn, and synchronized mechanical arms pass threads over and under one another.\n\nAs the robots continuously weave, a long horizontal sheet of luxurious metallic-gold fabric grows outward between them. The fabric is physically constructed strand by strand, with visible interlacing threads, realistic tension, ripples, folds, and shimmering woven texture. Do not generate a vertical banner.\n\nFrom 00:04 onward, the camera tracks smoothly above the expanding horizontal fabric while both robots continue weaving at the left and right sides of the frame. The weaving action remains visible throughout.\n\nFrom 00:06 onward, the Raylight emblem from <Picture 2> and the MiniMax emblem from <Picture 3> gradually emerge as two separate woven patterns inside the gold fabric. The logos are not projected, printed, pasted, floating, or glowing above the surface; their shapes are physically formed by contrasting threads integrated into the textile weave.\n\nAt 00:09, the camera reaches a symmetrical overhead hero composition showing both robots, their moving mechanical hands, the complete long horizontal gold fabric, and both clearly recognizable woven logos. End while the loom and robot hands are still moving.\n\nSound: precise metallic finger clicks, rotating gears, fast loom clacks, fabric tension sounds, and a low futuristic mechanical hum. No dialogue.\n\nAvoid: robot transformation sequence, fighting, weapons, laser beams, cloth appearing instantly, vertical fabric, sewing with needles, logos floating above the cloth, logos appearing as screens or projections, unreadable duplicate logos, extra robots, distorted hands, soft toy-like robots, dark underexposed image, camera cuts that hide the weaving action."
      ],
      "color": "#322",
      "bgcolor": "#533"
    },
